DECODELABS Week 1 – Data Cleaning
Project Overview
As part of my Data Analytics Internship at DECODELABS, I completed a data cleaning project using Microsoft Excel and Power Query.The objective of the project was to prepare a raw e-commerce dataset for analysis by identifying and addressing data quality issues such as missing values, duplicates, and incorrect data formats.
Dataset
•	Rows: 1,200
•	Columns: 14
•	Dataset type: E-commerce order data
Data Cleaning Process
The dataset was imported into Power Query Editor in Microsoft Excel, where I carried out the following checks and cleaning activities:
1. Data Type Check
I reviewed the data types of all 14 columns.
All columns had appropriate data types, so no data type corrections were required.
2. Duplicate Check
I checked the dataset for duplicate Order IDs.
No duplicate records were identified, and all 1,200 records were retained.
3. Missing Values
The Coupon Code column contained missing values.
•	Missing Coupon Code values: 309
•	Percentage of missing values: 25%
To make the dataset easier to analyze, the missing values were replaced with "NO COUPON".
4. Final Dataset
After completing the cleaning process, the cleaned dataset was loaded back into Excel for further analysis.
Tools Used
•	Microsoft Excel
•	Power Query
Key Outcome
The data cleaning process produced a structured and analysis-ready dataset. The cleaned dataset was subsequently used for Week 2: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA).
Skills Demonstrated
•	Data cleaning
•	Missing value handling
•	Duplicate detection
•	Data quality checking
•	Power Query
•	Excel data preparation
